; Rust's `wrapping_div` returned `INT_MIN`. Added `c_int_div` using `cdq; idiv` inline asm → release build now emits the identical `cltd; idiv %esi`.\n2. `find_and_replace_char(NULL, …)` — C **SIGSEGV**, Rust **SIGABRT** (rustc's debug null-deref check → non-unwinding panic). All raw byte access now goes through `read_volatile`/`write_volatile`.\n3. Same for `process_octal_string(NULL, …)`.\n\n## Phase D — completion gate\n- Symbol diff empty for every artifact pair; suite passes over the whole matrix {Rust dev, Rust release `panic=abort`} × {C `-O0`, C `-O2`} in the single feature configuration (`./verify_all.sh`: **ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED**, 52 tests/run, stable over repeated runs and `--test-threads=1/4/16`).\n- Brute-force sweeps (`RUN_EXHAUSTIVE=1`): **all 2³²** inputs of `validate_and_normalize`, 9.4 M values of `process_octal_string`, 17 M needles of `find_and_replace_char`, `operation_count` overflow past `INT_MAX`, and a 300 000-step whole-API fuzz (600 000 transcript lines, `cmp`-clean).\n- **Harness validated by mutation testing:** 13 hand-built mutants of `src/lib.rs` (threshold off-by-ones, `'X'→'Y'`, `%o→%x`, dropped `operation_count++`, floor vs truncating division, sentinel change, guard flips) were all killed.\n- An independent audit agent re-derived the comparison from scratch (its own C dlopen drivers, full 2³² sweeps of `process_octal_string` and the needle conversion, fork-per-case `findrep` state checks) and found **no divergences**; I re-ran two of its shards myself (0 diffs) and confirmed its Rust `.so` copies were built from the current source and contain the `idiv` fix.\n\nOne documented, target-specific caveat: on non-x86-64 targets `c_int_div` falls back to `wrapping_div` (those ISAs' signed divide doesn't trap), noted in the code and `ERRORS.md`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":191217,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":587,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e32b10b8-2a5f-4856-b089-d80616d51352","uuid":"d734c800-6c96-42e5-a74e-db4cbd02185d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T20:17:30.761Z"}
